WEBVTT

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:06.310
German Democratic Republic 
Bebersee Base

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:06.310
Schwarzes-02 took a serious hit from 
nine o'clock and went down.

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:10.060
Second Lieutenant Waldheim got too far 
ahead, and she went to protect her,

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:12.350
but a Grappler-class shot her down.

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:14.750
We should go rescue them now!

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:17.560
HQ hasn't issued any orders.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.170
But if we don't do something...

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.800
Repair and resupply is our current priority.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.580
There are still Laser-classes alive.

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:28.090
Theodor, you're okay with this?

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:29.940
It doesn't bother you?

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:32.010
Your comrades might die!

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:33.970
It has nothing to do with me.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:37.610
Don't give me that! 
You're her trainer, aren't you?

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:39.760
And what am I supposed to do?

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:40.810
You...

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:43.430
Stop it, would you?

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.940
Comrades?

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:50.470
You just want to atone for letting Second 
Lieutenant Inghild die, don't you?

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:52.760
Don't get others caught up in it.

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:55.170
Stop it, Sylwia.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:58.200
And it'd be a waste of time to go, anyway.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:01.190
They won't be coming back.

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:03.260
Neither of them.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:44.140
German Democratic Republic 
Fort Neuenhagen

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:46.330
I'm Sergeant Major Kurt Griebel, 
of the 500th Jaeger Corps.

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:49.910
This is Sergeant Vivian Schweinsteiger.

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:52.720
Thank you for saving me.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:54.650
We were just carrying out our mission.

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:59.530
TSF pilots aren't replaceable, 
like infantry are.

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:02.410
But the BETA ate an entire platoon.

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:06.120
We don't blame you.

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:08.810
I'll show you the escape route.

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:09.790
Come with us.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:17.480
Wow!

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:19.750
This really is a fortress.

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:23.310
This place is cut off from the other forts.

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:25.050
It's natural that it would be surrounded,

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:27.970
so it's built tough.

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:31.190
We can't let them break through, you know.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.700
Is that...

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:43.830
It is.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:45.720
Our capital, Berlin.

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:50.250
Everyone's probably eating dinner 
in their heated homes right now.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:53.240
It's so close to the battlefield.

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:57.000
The government won't let anyone evacuate.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:06.850
That'd be like admitting defeat.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:09.260
And because of the Stasi, no one can complain.

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:12.050
They know they're doomed,

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:14.950
but they cling to the fantasy that 
everything will work out,

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:17.900
and try their best to live peaceful lives.

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:22.250
If we die, that place becomes a battlefield.

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:27.910
So we must fight here,
with every single thing we've got.

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:33.890
We're pawns to be sacrificed so that the 
fortress will stand a few more moments.

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:35.730
We're expendable.

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:39.270
But that's fine.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:42.130
As long as we can protect those lights.

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:55.330
Lights...

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:08.100
Daddy!

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.200
Go, you two!

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:13.570
Theodor, take care of Lise!

00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:15.240
Mom! Dad!

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:16.320
Don't worry about me!

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:17.280
Go!

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:18.500
Let's go, Lise!

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:21.550
Lise! Lise!

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:23.910
Brother!

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:28.180
Eberbach, I'll see you later.

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:39.940
Take care of her.

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:47.250
<i>I don't want trouble.</i>

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:52.870
It doesn't matter to me what happens to her.

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:57.460
The Stasi gave that order?

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:01.460
They demanded transfer of command 
authority in exchange for their support.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:06.180
But military police reinforcements never came.

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:09.460
Maintenance trouble with 
the Cheburashkas, they said.

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:11.350
That's an obvious lie!

00:06:11.780 --> 00:06:15.380
Are they trying to start a fight with 
the National People's Army?

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:18.980
They essentially killed Major Hannibal!

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:23.980
They may want to wear down the NPA's strength.

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:28.150
Anyway, now that they've separated Second 
Lieutenant Waldheim from the squadron,

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:30.450
they can do whatever they want with her.

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:33.750
Take care, Gretel.

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:36.120
This is my warning to you, as a friend.

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:39.080
All right, Marai.

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:44.000
<i>Those Stasi scum!</i>

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:47.720
<i>Why are they so interested in 
Second Lieutenant Waldheim?</i>

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:49.260
It can't be...

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:57.350
There you are.

00:06:58.260 --> 00:07:00.480
I need to talk to you. Come with me.

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:06.180
What are you hiding?

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:08.540
Don't play dumb!

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:10.360
I'm talking about Katia Waldheim.

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:17.170
The Stasi's plan was probably intended to 
separate the comrade lieutenant from us.

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:17.870
No way.

00:07:18.570 --> 00:07:19.350
Tell me.

00:07:19.350 --> 00:07:22.530
What are you and Captain Bernhard hiding?

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:23.610
Nothing.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:28.780
I'm just looking out for her because 
the comrade captain ordered me to.

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:33.160
If the comrade captain is covering for that 
kid because of some traitorous plan,

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:34.510
this won't end well at all!

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:36.890
Why are you talking about the comrade captain?

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:41.140
"Traitorous"?

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:43.210
She's a dog of the Stasi, isn't she?

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:45.790
Tell me.

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:47.480
What's going on?

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:50.740
Even if you knew, there's nothing you can do.

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:54.160
The Moonlit Night Incident.

00:07:54.700 --> 00:08:00.280
A coup d'état five years ago, by 
anti-establishment, high-ranking officers.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:05.650
It failed, but they were planning to bring 
down Germany's Socialist Unity Party,

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:07.920
as well as the Stasi.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.630
Who would do such a thing?

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:12.840
The hero that once protected East Germany.

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:15.640
The former commander of the 1st Tank Corps,

00:08:16.170 --> 00:08:18.890
Lieutenant General Alfred Strachwitz.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:21.700
You know him?

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:23.290
N-No...

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:24.480
I'm sure.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:28.900
That name, as well as the incident 
itself, was erased by the Stasi.

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:33.770
You think she's a dog of the Stasi?

00:08:35.150 --> 00:08:37.030
She turned in her family...

00:08:37.420 --> 00:08:39.410
That can't be true.

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:42.790
She's too honest.

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:47.680
She has incredible self-discipline, and on the 
battlefield, she's always first to charge in.

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:49.800
She cares for her troops and unites them.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:53.530
I can't believe she's the kind of scum 
who would sell out her family.

00:08:53.940 --> 00:08:58.310
And the fact that she hasn't informed 
on anyone but her brother proves it.

00:08:58.310 --> 00:08:59.300
Then...

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:02.410
She was probably allowed to live...

00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:12.530
...by her brother's will.

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:19.540
The heir to her brother's 
anti-establishment ideology

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:25.330
is now commander of East Germany's 
strongest TSF squadron.

00:09:26.090 --> 00:09:29.500
Do you think that's just a coincidence?

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:41.560
They're coming!

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:46.040
Aim for the legs!

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:47.320
Stop them!

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:48.340
Roger!

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:53.630
You're in the way! Move!

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:55.780
Sergeant, take her and get back!

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:56.070
Right!

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:58.610
Don't die, Sergeant Major!

00:10:00.610 --> 00:10:01.250
Let's go!

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:02.120
O-Okay!

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:04.120
Everyone, keep firing!

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:06.630
Support the main flank of the reinforcements!

00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:17.500
What do you want, Comrade Lieutenant?

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:19.000
You look pale.

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:20.550
Are you sleeping okay?

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:23.780
I've learned a lot about you.

00:10:24.340 --> 00:10:25.390
What?

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:27.420
About the coup d'état.

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:30.250
About Lieutenant General Strachwitz.

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:33.400
And the reason you shot your own brother.

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:35.610
I have no idea what you mean.

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:39.220
But a coup d'état is a serious matter.

00:10:39.220 --> 00:10:42.130
I may have to report you to the Stasi—

00:10:42.130 --> 00:10:43.560
Stop it.

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:45.120
You're not the type.

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:47.300
How can you be so sure?

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:49.610
I'm a dog of the Stasi.

00:10:49.610 --> 00:10:51.880
If you were, you wouldn't try

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:54.570
to protect Katia, Strachwitz's daughter!

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:57.260
She came back because she 
wanted to see her father,

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:59.890
which is the most natural thing in the world.

00:10:59.890 --> 00:11:03.200
She came to this hell of a country, 
without regard for danger!

00:11:04.870 --> 00:11:07.590
She's not like me...

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:12.350
I was tortured by the Stasi.

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:17.720
And I was so scared of them, I told them 
everything they wanted me to say.

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:25.870
I sold out my parents 
because I wanted to survive.

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:29.870
I'm sick of it.

00:11:30.530 --> 00:11:33.200
Sick of seeing those who do 
the right thing get crushed,

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:36.750
and of losing the people I care about.

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:38.710
I...

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:42.720
No matter what you want, 
if you give up, you'll never get it!

00:11:44.590 --> 00:11:48.020
I don't want to give up anymore!

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:58.450
I've been waiting for this, Theodor Eberbach.

00:11:59.730 --> 00:12:02.960
I'm on your side.

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:08.920
Not a people for the country,

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:10.630
but a country for the people.

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:14.260
No more Stasi spies, no informants, no purges.

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:16.840
We'll turn it back into a free, righteous country.

00:12:17.350 --> 00:12:20.340
That was Lieutenant General Strachwitz's wish.

00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:24.370
My life doesn't belong to me alone.

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:28.330
The lieutenant general, my brother, 
my friends who were purged...

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:32.230
It belongs to all those who entrusted 
me with their hopes.

00:12:32.950 --> 00:12:37.230
No matter what happens to me, 
I have a duty to save East Germany.

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:39.360
That's why you care about Katia.

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:43.280
But why have a horrible person 
like me take care of her?

00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:47.990
Because I believe you will never abandon Katia.

00:12:48.630 --> 00:12:51.540
Because you lost your little sister to the Stasi.

00:12:52.470 --> 00:12:55.000
So you know everything, huh?

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:57.550
Now that I've told you everything,

00:12:57.550 --> 00:13:01.910
I'll treat you as a comrade who shares my goals.

00:13:01.910 --> 00:13:02.850
That's okay, right?

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:06.010
What's wrong?

00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:08.110
I'm scared.

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:13.330
I'm scared I'll give in to the Stasi's torture, 
and sell someone out again.

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:15.520
When I think of that...

00:13:17.180 --> 00:13:20.050
People repeat their mistakes 
because of weakness.

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:22.740
No one can escape that sin.

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:26.780
Not me, not you, not anyone.

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:31.640
But that doesn't mean the 
last light will be tainted.

00:13:31.640 --> 00:13:33.990
The last light?

00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:38.790
This country is within darkness,
with no view of its future,

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:40.790
and no one to believe in.

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:47.090
The one light in that darkness is a heart 
that wants to save and protect someone.

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:52.850
Vivi!

00:13:59.990 --> 00:14:01.860
Vivi...

00:14:07.710 --> 00:14:08.820
Vivi!

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:10.770
Take this!

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:14.830
No...

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:16.870
No!

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:20.880
What is your wish?

00:14:22.070 --> 00:14:24.420
I want to protect Katia.

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:29.010
Then I will help you.

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:32.730
So save her from despair,

00:14:33.190 --> 00:14:36.060
Pilot Theodor Eberbach!

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:45.360
Attention, all units.

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:47.700
The order to launch again has been given.

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:50.410
We will now execute a laserjagd against the

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:54.030
Laser-classes in the BETA echelon 
west of the Oder River.

00:14:54.730 --> 00:14:57.290
Um, what about reinforcing Fort Neuenhagen?

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:58.320
Not happening.

00:14:58.320 --> 00:15:01.330
Our sole objective is to 
eliminate the Laser-classes.

00:15:01.690 --> 00:15:03.030
The laserjagd.

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:04.290
No...

00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:07.300
We will fulfill our mission. That is all.

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:10.940
666th Squadron, Schwarzesmarken,

00:15:10.940 --> 00:15:12.260
launch!

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:21.480
Heavy-metal cloud density readings increasing.

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:25.280
It's highly probable that 
communications will be blocked.

00:15:25.280 --> 00:15:26.360
Stay in formation.

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:29.110
By the way, Comrade Lieutenant...

00:15:30.270 --> 00:15:34.090
When contact with command is lost 
beneath the heavy-metal clouds,

00:15:34.090 --> 00:15:37.240
how are TSF squadrons to be controlled?

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:39.600
Why are we going over this now?

00:15:40.360 --> 00:15:44.040
Full authority is given to the squadron 
commander and political commissar,

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:47.250
but as long as the mission is fulfilled, 
any necessary means—

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:48.950
No way!

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:51.930
Attention, all units.

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:54.140
Our squadron will now split its forces.

00:15:54.530 --> 00:15:57.640
I will lead a platoon to the laserjagd.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:16:01.640
And one squad will head to Fort Neuenhagen.

00:16:01.970 --> 00:16:04.550
What are you thinking, Comrade Captain?

00:16:04.550 --> 00:16:07.860
As long as the mission is fulfilled, 
any means will be allowed, correct?

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:10.110
That's not what it means!

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:13.540
Second Lieutenant Theodor Eberbach 
volunteers for the 2nd squad.

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:14.040
What?

00:16:15.050 --> 00:16:16.780
I'll go, too.

00:16:17.030 --> 00:16:19.800
If we're going in, Theodor and I are specialized

00:16:19.800 --> 00:16:22.020
for close-range combat, so we should go.

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:22.790
You...

00:16:23.770 --> 00:16:25.870
You idiots!

00:16:25.870 --> 00:16:28.070
I will take full responsibility.

00:16:28.070 --> 00:16:28.850
Go!

00:16:28.850 --> 00:16:30.030
Roger!

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:31.160
Comrade Captain,

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:32.330
you can't!

00:16:32.330 --> 00:16:35.610
We will proceed, as planned, 
to execute the laserjagd.

00:16:36.170 --> 00:16:38.560
Time for the hunt you've been waiting for.

00:16:41.950 --> 00:16:43.850
Fire! Fire!

00:16:50.600 --> 00:16:52.730
My leg... My leg!

00:16:52.730 --> 00:16:55.040
Erich! Get up, Erich!

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:56.310
He's already dead!

00:16:57.430 --> 00:16:58.870
What are you doing?

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:01.620
Vivi... Vivi is...

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:04.110
Stand. Stand and fight!

00:17:04.110 --> 00:17:09.210
I didn't know anything 
about the real battlefield...

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:15.720
If both Germanys, East and 
West, worked together,

00:17:17.130 --> 00:17:19.470
I actually thought we could beat the BETA.

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:21.640
That's right. This is reality.

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:23.830
But you're a pilot.

00:17:23.830 --> 00:17:27.440
If you're a pilot, you can save many 
more people than we can.

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:29.480
So you have to survive!

00:17:38.630 --> 00:17:39.720
Kurt!

00:17:50.960 --> 00:17:52.520
Eberbach...

00:17:55.980 --> 00:17:56.930
Katia!

00:18:06.380 --> 00:18:07.770
Get in, you two!

00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:09.540
Theodor?

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:11.770
But Kurt...

00:18:12.590 --> 00:18:16.240
G-Get going...

00:18:18.430 --> 00:18:22.310
Never come to a place like this again.

00:18:23.140 --> 00:18:24.290
Kurt...

00:18:30.100 --> 00:18:34.790
Kurt, I'm a pilot.

00:18:36.020 --> 00:18:41.830
I'll fight to save as many as I can.

00:19:03.890 --> 00:19:05.840
Sergeant Major! Sergeant Major!

00:19:07.240 --> 00:19:11.160
I found some ammunition in the 262nd 
warehouse that isn't in the ledgers!

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:14.800
Nice work.

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:17.450
I'll give you some chocolate later as a reward.

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:20.510
The good American stuff.

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:21.970
Yay!

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:20.490
I see... So that's what my father did.

00:20:32.970 --> 00:20:35.910
It's only a matter of time until 
this country is destroyed.

00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:40.740
But if we defeat the Stasi and work 
with the Western nations,

00:20:40.740 --> 00:20:41.580
perhaps...

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:44.000
Katia...

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:45.010
Yes.

00:20:45.270 --> 00:20:47.830
You are the daughter of 
Lieutenant General Strachwitz,

00:20:47.830 --> 00:20:50.010
and you know both East and West Germany.

00:20:50.490 --> 00:20:53.100
You may be able to be a bridge 
between East and West.

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:57.640
Theodor, look after Katia.

00:20:57.640 --> 00:20:58.610
Comrade Captain...

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:02.390
Call me "Irisdina."

00:21:06.110 --> 00:21:06.920
Katia...

00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:11.500
I'll protect you, no matter what.

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:13.690
Theodor...

00:21:21.250 --> 00:21:23.900
If something happens to me,

00:21:23.900 --> 00:21:26.050
I'll call your name three times.

00:21:31.270 --> 00:21:32.060
This is...

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:35.450
Somewhere in 
East Berlin

00:23:14.390 --> 00:23:18.450
German Democratic Republic 
Bebersee Base

00:23:17.340 --> 00:23:19.330
U-Um...

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:20.420
Yes?

00:23:20.810 --> 00:23:25.400
Is the 666th Squadron's captain here?

00:23:25.400 --> 00:23:28.080
I've come here as a replacement, 
and I'll be starting today.

00:23:28.080 --> 00:23:31.680
Huh? Oh... Okay, come in.

00:23:32.480 --> 00:23:35.830
I didn't know we had anyone coming.

00:23:37.160 --> 00:23:39.990
My name is Katia Waldheim.

00:23:39.990 --> 00:23:42.580
I haven't been here long myself,

00:23:42.580 --> 00:23:44.360
so let's get along.

00:23:46.550 --> 00:23:48.820
Lise Hohenstein.

00:23:48.820 --> 00:23:51.110
Nice to meet you, Katia.

00:23:51.820 --> 00:23:55.750
<b>To Be Continued</b>
